# C1 regression: the quotepath bypass. An accepted ADR is renamed (git mv, so
# git detects it as R) to a NON-ASCII filename AND its frozen body is edited,
# then the manifest is regenerated so the manifest cross-check is satisfied by
# the tampered content. Before the fix, `git diff --name-status` C-quoted the
# non-ASCII path (arriving as "...premi\303\250re-r\303\250gle.md" — a literal
# string ending in `.md"`, not `.md`), so the extension filter silently
# skipped it and, with the manifest regenerated, guard reported clean exit 0 —
# a full evasion. With `-z` (raw NUL-delimited paths) the rename is seen for
# what it is: file_renamed AND the smuggled body_changed both fire. Exit 1.
#
# Deliberately asserts NO manifest_mismatch: the attacker defeated the manifest
# by regenerating it, so this is git mode alone catching the bypass — exactly
# the path C1 said was broken.

env CONSTITUTION_TODAY=2026-07-01
env GIT_AUTHOR_NAME=guard-test
env GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL=guard-test@example.com
env GIT_COMMITTER_NAME=guard-test
env GIT_COMMITTER_EMAIL=guard-test@example.com
env GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1

exec git init -q -b main
exec constitution adr new --title 'First rule' --body-file body.md
exec git add -A
exec git commit -q -m init

# rename to a non-ASCII filename (git mv stages it so -M reports R, not D+add),
# smuggle a frozen-body edit under the rename, then regenerate the manifest so
# the manifest cross-check is satisfied by the tampered content.
exec git mv constitution/adr/ADR-0001-first-rule.md constitution/adr/ADR-0001-première-règle.md
cp tampered.md constitution/adr/ADR-0001-première-règle.md
exec constitution regen

exitcode 1 constitution guard
stdout '\[file_renamed\] ADR-0001'
stdout '\[body_changed\] ADR-0001'
! stdout 'manifest_mismatch'

# and the JSON payload carries both kinds against the true (unquoted) path
exitcode 1 constitution guard --format json
stdout '"kind": "file_renamed"'
stdout '"kind": "body_changed"'
stdout 'ADR-0001-première-règle.md'
stdout '"clean": false'

-- constitution.yml --
schemaVersion: 1
phase: sealed
consent:
  policy: off
sourceTracking:
  type: none
categories:
  - architecture

-- body.md --
## Context and Problem Statement

We need a governing rule.

## Considered Options

- Do nothing
- Adopt the rule

## Decision Outcome

Adopt the rule.

-- tampered.md --
---
id: ADR-0001
title: First rule
category: architecture
date: 2026-07-01
status: accepted
---

## Context and Problem Statement

We need a governing rule.

## Considered Options

- Do nothing
- Adopt the rule

## Decision Outcome

Quietly reverse the rule.
